+# hud_edge, compiled from hud_edge.c (hud_edge at +0) with
+# aarch64-none-linux-gnu-gcc -O2 -ffreestanding -fno-builtin -fno-stack-protector
+# -fno-jump-tables -fno-asynchronous-unwind-tables -c -- the same flags 0113's
+# hud_calc used. The function takes everything through its arguments (no static
+# data, no literal pool, no external calls), so these words are position-independent
+# and relocation-free and can be dropped into the rewriter's patch area verbatim:
+#   x0 = the pane, x1 = the aspect (a pointer to state page + 0x58: the screen
+#   aspect ratio r, written there by dm_fps_state_apply in loader.c -- 0 when the
+#   screen is 16:9, the window's aspect otherwise, so "auto" already resolves to
+#   the real aspect before the hook runs), x2 = table (state page + 0x300, eight
+#   120-byte entries, two per HUD element). No log buffer: nothing is logged.
+# Element order: 0 compass, 1 life, 2 coins, 3 moons.
+# What it does, per pane: it matches the four HUD elements by pane NAME only
+# ('PicStrap' = compass, 'Life' = lives, 'TxtCounterSh' / 'TxtCounter' = coins,
+# 'Counter' / 'TxtTotalShine' = moons, 'TxtLife' = lives) and translates each by a
+# FIXED horizontal offset computed from the aspect at runtime:
+#   edge = 640 * (aspect / 1.7777778 - 1), clamped to [-200, +200] UI px.
+#   aspect 2.167 (iPhone 19.5:9): edge +140 -- coins/moons move LEFT (-140),
+#     compass/lives move RIGHT (+140), to the screen edges.
+#   aspect 1.429 (iPhone Duo 1.43:1): edge -126 -- the HUD is laid out for 16:9,
+#     so on the narrower screen it would be cut off; coins/moons move RIGHT (+126),
+#     compass/lives move LEFT (-126), pulled in to the edges.
+#   aspect 1.333 (iPad 4:3): edge -160 -- coins/moons +160, compass/lives -160.
+#   aspect 1.778 (16:9) or 0: edge 0, a no-op. The dy is always 0 and the scale
+#   is never touched: translation only, never a resize. See hud_edge.c for the
+#   layouts and the design (orig/mod table, no-drift, game-recompute follow,
+#   the dirty flag so a moved container carries its children, the bounded
+#   mark-dirty walk).
